Lena — An Emacs major mode for Lean
***********************************

Lena is a set of packages that extend GNU Emacs
(https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/) for the Lean
(https://lean-lang.org) language.  It is based off Nael
(https://codeberg.org/mekeor/nael) additionally providing an infoview,
signs in the margin and more.  See *note Credits: Credits. for more
information about Lena's lineage.

   Lena is not on Elpa or Melpa yet.  To install Lena, use ‘package-vc’
or a clone of this repository, see *note Install: Install. for detailed
instructions.

   *Note*: Much of the code that Lena adds to Nael was written with the
help of AI assistants and reviewed, tested and revised by Lena's
maintainers.

