4.1.1 Manual
------------

First clone the Git repository, then, in your Emacs initialization file,
add Lena to ‘load-path’ and load it.  For lazy loading the
autoloads-file needs to be built beforehand.

     ;; git clone https://github.com/ISTA-PLV/lena.git ~/path/to/lena

     (add-to-list 'load-path "~/path/to/lena/lena")
     ;; For Evil:
     ;; (add-to-list 'load-path "~/path/to/lena/lena-evil")

     ;; Option 1, eager loading:
     (require 'lena)
     ;; (require 'lena-evil)

     ;; Option 2, lazy loading:
     ;; cd ~/path/to/lena && ./build.el autoloads
     ;; (require 'lena-autoloads)
     ;; (require 'lena-evil-autoloads)

     ;; Optionally, make the README available as an Info manual:
     (require 'info)
     (info-initialize)
     (add-to-list 'Info-directory-list "~/path/to/lena/lena")


