4.3.1 Flymake and Margin
------------------------

The signs in the margin can be changed, for example, with chickens
below.  Play around with the value for ‘lena-margin-emoji-height’ to
scale your chosen characters to the line height.

     (setq lena-margin-goals-accomplished "🐣"  ; complete proof
           lena-margin-unsolved-goals "🥚"      ; unsolved goals
           lena-margin-admitted "🍗"            ; uses sorry
           lena-margin-emoji-height 1)          ; as tall as text lines

   To keep Flymake's indicators instead of the signs, set ‘lena-margin’
to ‘nil’, before visiting a Lean file.

   Lena truncates the trace of Flymake, only showing "(trace)", as in VS
Code.  To keep the full text in Flymake instead, set
‘lena-eglot-widgets’ to ‘nil’ before Lean starts.

   To start Lean buffers with the input method off, set
‘lena-activate-quail’ to ‘nil’; ‘C-\’ still turns it on.  To keep your
global default input method instead, set ‘lena-prepare-quail’ to ‘nil’.


