6 Credits
*********

Lena builds on the ideas and code of many other projects in order to
provide the experience it does now.  In particular,
   • Lena is forked off Nael (https://codeberg.org/mekeor/nael),
   • dependency management and ‘lena-rpc.el’ are adapted from Doug
     Torrance's lean4-mode (https://github.com/d-torrance/lean4-mode),
     and _Jan Mas Rovira_'s neo-lean-mode
     (https://github.com/janmasrovira/neo-lean-mode),
   • Lena's input method is generated from vscode-lean4
     (https://github.com/leanprover/vscode-lean4),
   • the infoview is modelled after lean.nvim
     (https://github.com/Julian/lean.nvim), and vscode-lean4
     (https://github.com/leanprover/vscode-lean4),
   • the test fixtures are from iris-lean
     (https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean)

   For a more detailed per-file breakdown, see the copyright header of
each file.


File: lena.info,  Node: License and Maintenance,  Prev: Credits,  Up: Top

7 License and Maintenance
*************************

Lena is effectively licensed under GNU GPL version 3 only.  More
precisely, the code that comes from Nael is licensed under Apache-2.0
and sublicensed under GPL-3.0.

   The files that Lena adds are licensed under GPL-3.0-only, except
‘lena-rpc.el’.  Parts of ‘lena-eglot.el’ are adapted from lean4-mode
(https://github.com/d-torrance/lean4-mode) under Apache-2.0.
‘lena-rpc.el’ is derived from lean4-mode and neo-lean-mode
(https://github.com/janmasrovira/neo-lean-mode) and licensed under the
MIT License, see ‘LICENSE.MIT’.  The smartparens pairs and the Doom
Emacs setup in this manual follow Doom Emacs' ‘:lang lean’ module, under
the MIT License.  The input method is generated from data of
vscode-lean4 (https://github.com/leanprover/vscode-lean4), under
Apache-2.0.  The test fixtures are recorded from iris-lean
(https://github.com/leanprover-community/iris-lean), under Apache-2.0.
For details, see ‘NOTICE’ and ‘test/fixtures/README.org’.

   Lena is maintained by _Klaus Kraßnitzer_ and _Alex Loitzl_ of ISTA
PLV at github.com/ISTA-PLV/lena (https://github.com/ISTA-PLV/lena);
please report problems there.


